{% comment %}
  Home-page hero, THIRD vignette (session 11): the real trimmed public
  playground itself (vZero/PublicDemo.tsx via `make static-demo`,
  assets/playground/), not a decorative single-file animation like
  hero-value-flow.liquid/hero-flow-field.liquid (this directory) -- those
  two stay untouched, per goal.md's "do not remove anything, just keep
  adding" instruction. This is a real classification playground: pick a
  dataset, edit the network, watch a real from-scratch MLP train live, right
  inside the iframe, no server involved (see vZero's own
  PublicDemo.tsx/engine/browser/* for what's actually running).

  Auto-sizing (fix for "the playground keeps moving" -- diagnosed empirically,
  see main-public.tsx's own comment): a fixed height guess here can never
  match the iframe's real content, which is viewport-width-dependent and was
  MEASURED at ~1939px at this embed's own 620x360 size -- height="360"
  scrolling="no" was clipping ~80% of the app, permanently unreachable. The
  iframe's own page (main-public.tsx) now posts its real content height via
  postMessage on load and on every resize; the listener below just applies
  it, so the iframe is always exactly as tall as its content -- one scroll
  container (this page), not two. height="360" below is only the BEFORE-JS
  fallback (first paint, or postMessage somehow blocked), not a claim of
  correctness on its own -- scrolling stays enabled (no scrolling="no") so
  that fallback is at least reachable via the iframe's own scrollbar rather
  than fully clipped.

  `?nostory=1` on the src (fix for a SECOND regression caught in review,
  before shipping): a first-time visitor -- i.e. every visitor landing on
  the home page, which is the entire point of a homepage hero -- has no
  `vzero-public-seen-v1` in localStorage, so PublicDemo.tsx defaults to
  StoryView, the 4-section scroll-driven explainer, not the actual "pick a
  dataset, edit the network, watch it train" teaser this include's own copy
  promises. Auto-sizing then correctly reported StoryView's real height
  (~4200px at this embed's 640px width) and the hero became a scroll-
  monster on the home page -- a different failure mode than the original
  360px clip, but still wrong. `?nostory=1` (PublicDemo.tsx's own
  `showStory` initializer) skips straight to Instrument for this embed
  specifically, the same way a returning visitor's localStorage flag
  already does; the full-page /playground/ embed does NOT pass this
  param, so first-time visitors there still see the explainer.
  MAX_HERO_HEIGHT below is a second, independent line of defense for this
  specific small teaser slot (not the full-page embed, which stays
  uncapped) -- a future content change here shouldn't be able to
  regress the home page into a tall block again even if `?nostory=1`
  itself were ever removed or bypassed; scrolling stays enabled precisely
  so hitting that cap degrades to "scroll within a small box," not clipping.

  Usage: {% include hero-playground.liquid %}
{% endcomment %}
<div class="hero-playground" style="margin: 1.5rem 0; max-width: 640px;">
  <iframe
    id="vzero-hero-playground-frame"
    src="{{ '/assets/playground/index.html' | relative_url }}?nostory=1"
    title="Live demo: the vZero Neural ODE playground, running entirely in your browser"
    width="100%"
    height="360"
    style="border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08); border-radius: 8px; display: block;"
    loading="lazy"
  >
  </iframe>
  <p style="margin-top: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.85rem;">
    <a href="{{ '/playground/' | relative_url }}">Open the full playground &rarr;</a>
  </p>
</div>
<script>
  (function () {
    var frame = document.getElementById('vzero-hero-playground-frame');
    if (!frame) return;
    // This teaser slot's own ceiling -- independent of the general
    // 200-6000 sanity bound below, and deliberately tighter: a homepage
    // hero has no business being taller than this regardless of what the
    // embedded page reports.
    var MAX_HERO_HEIGHT = 700;
    window.addEventListener('message', function (event) {
      if (event.source !== frame.contentWindow) return;
      var data = event.data;
      if (!data || data.source !== 'vzero-playground' || data.type !== 'resize') return;
      var h = Number(data.height);
      if (!isFinite(h) || h <= 0) return;
      // Sane bounds: never below a stubby sliver, never past a degenerate
      // runaway value (a real bug elsewhere shouldn't grow this unbounded),
      // and never past this teaser's own MAX_HERO_HEIGHT ceiling.
      h = Math.max(200, Math.min(h, MAX_HERO_HEIGHT));
      frame.style.height = h + 'px';
    });
  })();
</script>
